{"name":"Sceptic","hex":"#9db4aa","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sceptic","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of skeptic."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative spelling of skeptic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sceptic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sceptic (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Sceptic is a death metal band from Kraków, Poland."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sceptic_(band)","wikidata":"Q769312"},{"title":"Skepticism","blocks":[{"text":"Skepticism (US) or scepticism (UK) is a questioning attitude or doubt toward knowledge claims that are seen as mere belief or dogma. For example, if a person is skeptical about claims made by their government about an ongoing war then the person doubts that these claims are accurate. In such cases, skeptics normally recommend not disbelief but suspension of belief, i.e. maintaining a neutral attitude that neither affirms nor denies the claim. This attitude is often motivated by the impression that the available evidence is insufficient to support the claim. Formally, skepticism is a topic of interest in philosophy, particularly epistemology."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skepticism","wikidata":"Q1395219"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Philosopher_marble_head_Roman_copy_AM_Corfu_Krfm22-removebg-preview.png/330px-Philosopher_marble_head_Roman_copy_AM_Corfu_Krfm22-removebg-preview.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Philosopher_marble_head_Roman_copy_AM_Corfu_Krfm22-removebg-preview.png/330px-Philosopher_marble_head_Roman_copy_AM_Corfu_Krfm22-removebg-preview.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhilosopher_marble_head_Roman_copy_AM_Corfu_Krfm22-removebg-preview.png"},{"srcset":"https://